{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1497523847,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDExMjQ4NzcwMjk="},"added":["feedback-desired"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1497523847,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDExMjQ4NzcwMzA="},"added":["question"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1497524457,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwODY5OTI5Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1582#issuecomment-308699292"},"message":"- Yes, I think, by default `install` and `get` should download content, that is `required`. Apart from what is considered to be the default, they need to be able to respect it.\n\n- This raises the question, whether `update` should consider it. If `required` changed it might get additional content ... Not sure about this one.\n\n- As discussed before, `publish` needs to respect those settings for the sibling to publish to, too.\n\n- May be `drop` needs a `--force` or something to drop it? (if `required`)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1497524770,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwODcwMDIyOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1582#issuecomment-308700228"},"message":"Additionally it might be nice to be able to specify that `drop`, `get`, `save`, `add` should respects only/all paths matching preferred content settings? Either a restriction to path specifications or an alternative specification of what to deal with (instead of path(s)).","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1497531721,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwODcyMjgyNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1582#issuecomment-308722825"},"message":"How could this be done in a uniform fashion. No path arguments would be confusing: `save` would no longer just save staged content.\n\nMaybe a generic `--auto(-content)`? But even that is not clear: `drop --auto` vs `get --auto` is drop all not wanted vs get all wanted.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1497531910,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwODcyMzU0OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1582#issuecomment-308723549"},"message":"Needs an explicit option - I agree.\nMay be like `--content='wanted'|'required'|...`?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1497533340,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwODcyOTI4NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1582#issuecomment-308729284"},"message":"what is the difference between `wanted` and `required`?\n\n`install` shouldn't get any data unless some option (ATM `-g` to get all the data) is given. \n `drop --auto` and `get --auto` make sense to me \n\nI wonder also if we need `--annex-get-opts` to pass arbitrary options to get while `install`.\n\nI also wonder if we might like to provide a \"path\" sugaring to `install`, so e.g. `datalad install ///openfmri/ds000006//sub-*/ses-*/anat` so we use `//` to indicate the boundary between dataset root and then a glob for paths.  (orthogonal to this) For install we are yet to figure out how to specify specific version (committish) to be installed.     I thought we had an issue for that but can't find ATM.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1497535004,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwODczNzMyOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1582#issuecomment-308737329"},"message":"`required` is 'hard-wanted' standard git-annex functionality.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1497537570,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwODc1MzcyMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1582#issuecomment-308753720"},"message":"`install shouldn't get any data unless some option (ATM -g to get all the data) is given.`\n\nRight! What I meant is: If there is `-g` then `--content` (in my notation - see above) could specify what data and default to `required`.\n\nEdit: Since `install -g` is calling `get` IIRC, this would be equal to specify `get --content=..` (with the same default). Looks consistent to me.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1543053546,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTM1NjM1NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1582#issuecomment-441356354"},"message":"Discussion can be considered over now","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1543053546,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTk4NDkzNzgyNA=="},"status":2}]}